"/*! a channel landing exactly on a \`.5\` boundary, which is the one place two
   engines round opposite ways (cssnano writes this hex too) */.t01{background:hsl(134,50%,50%)}/*! ...and one landing near enough to it for the same disagreement */.t02{background:hwb(194 0% 0%)}/*! ...and a Lab channel within the wider margin the matrix chain needs */.t03{background:lab(20% 40 0)}/*! a color outside the sRGB gamut, which the hex clips rather than respells */.t04{background:lab(50% 100 -100)}/*! ...whichever function names it */.t05{background:oklch(90% .3 140)}/*! ...including a predefined space wider than sRGB */.t06{background:color(display-p3 1 0 0)}/*! ...and one carrying an alpha, where the hex takes a fourth pair */.t07{background:lch(50% 130 20 / .5)}/*! a mix is the color it computes to, so it converts on the same terms */.t08{background:color-mix(in lch,white,lab(50% 100 -100))}/*! ...as does a relative color */.t09{background:oklch(from red calc(l*1.4) c h)}/*! declined still: an engine reads these two through a transfer of its own, so
   the hex would name a color it never paints rather than a near one */.t10{background:color(a98-rgb .2 .4 .6)}/*! ...both of them */.t11{background:color(prophoto-rgb .2 .4 .6)}/*! a color the conversion is exact for needs no option and takes none */.t12{background:red}/*! declined still: a hex this near gray loses its hue when mixed in \`oklch\`,
   where Chromium reads it as missing below a chroma of 0.02 */.t13{background:oklch(97.807% .029 256.847)}/*! ...as does one the conversion is exact for */.t14{background:oklch(97.4% .0159 227)}"
`;

