"/*! the hex before it is read by nothing: every target reads \`lab()\` */.t01{color:#c65d06;color:lab(50% 100 -100)}/*! ...whichever color function stands last */.t02{color:#7d2181;color:oklch(90% .3 140)}/*! ...and whatever the earlier one was spelled as */.t03{color:red;color:lch(50% 130 20)}/*! ...including where the later one is \`!important\` */.t04{color:red;color:oklch(90% .3 140)!important}/*! ...and where its arguments are colors this can name, a plain hex among them
   (which is what a \`light-dark()\` pair is written as) */.t04a{color:red;color:light-dark(#fff,#000)}/*! a keyword the property's own grammar names is the same question */.t05{display:block;display:flex}/*! ...however much newer it is */.t06{overflow:hidden;overflow:clip}/*! ...and however the target spells it */.t07{width:auto;width:fit-content}/*! declined: an \`!important\` earlier one wins wherever it is read, so it is the
   later one that carries nothing */.t08{color:red!important;color:oklch(90% .3 140)}/*! declined: \`canvastext\` carries no row of its own, and the ancient
   \`<system-color>\` it is filed under answers for the names of its own age
   rather than for this one */.t09{color:red;color:canvastext}/*! declined: the space a \`color()\` names is a keyword this cannot answer for,
   so the whole value is left unknown */.t10{color:red;color:color(display-p3 1 0 0)}/*! declined: ...as is a relative color, whose origin is no argument of the
   kind this reads */.t11{color:red;color:oklch(from red l c h)}/*! declined: a mix names its space and its colors as keywords, and the space is
   one of the unknown ones */.t12{color:red;color:color-mix(in oklch,red,blue)}/*! declined: a transition list keeps its dead prefixed entry, since dropping
   it shortens every list \`getComputedStyle\` reads off the shorthand */.t13{transition:transform.15s linear,-webkit-transform.15s linear}/*! declined: \`at\` cannot follow a color stop, so the later gradient is invalid
   and the earlier one is what every engine reads */.t14{background-image:linear-gradient(red,blue);background-image:radial-gradient(red at center,blue)}/*! declined: a trailing comma leaves an empty argument, which makes the later
   gradient invalid, so the earlier one stays */.t15{background-image:linear-gradient(red,blue);background-image:linear-gradient(red,blue,)}/*! a vendor spelling written before its standard twin is dead behind it */.t16{-moz-transform:scale(2);transform:scale(1)}/*! declined: one written after it, and important, is what Firefox reads,
   since it still takes the vendor name as an alias of the standard one */.t17{transform:scale(1);-moz-transform:scale(1.0001)!important}/*! ...though one after it saying the same thing is dead all the same */.t18{transform:scale(1);-moz-transform:scale(1)}"
`;

