   other, so they apply here too */.t10{width:16px;height:33.3333333%}/*! a media feature keeps the \`min-\`/\`max-\` spelling every engine reads */@media (min-width:1200px){.t06{color:red}}/*! ...at any nesting depth */@media ((min-width:1px) and (max-height:2px)){.t07{color:red}}/*! the \`inset\` shorthand is newer than the four longhands it merges */.t11{top:1px;right:2px;bottom:1px;left:2px}/*! ...unlike \`margin\`, whose shorthand is as old as its longhands */.t12{margin:1px 2px}/*! ...and a source \`inset\` is written as the four longhands it sets */.t13{top:1px;right:1px;bottom:1px;left:1px}/*! a two-position color stop is CSS Images 4, so the two stops stay */.t14{background-image:linear-gradient(red 0%,red 50%,blue)}/*! ...unlike the last stop's position, which CSS Images 3's own fix-up already
   puts there */.t15{background-image:linear-gradient(red,blue)}/*! the \`place-*\` shorthands are newer than the pairs they merge */.t16{align-items:center;justify-items:end}.t17{align-self:center;justify-self:center}.t18{align-content:center;justify-content:end}/*! ...unlike \`gap\`, whose shorthand is as old as its longhands */.t19{gap:1px 2px}/*! ...and a source \`place-items\` is written as the two longhands it sets */.t20{align-items:center;justify-items:end}/*! ...and two-value \`overflow\`, which Chrome 50 predates */.t21{overflow-x:hidden;overflow-y:scroll}/*! ...while collapsing it to one value is as old as the longhands */.t22{overflow:hidden}"
`;

