"/*! the first statement of a layer is where it sits in the cascade, so a later
   copy of it never stands in for it */@layer first;.t01{color:red}@layer first;/*! a keyframe selector is read under the rule it is written in */@keyframes t02{0%{opacity:0}to{opacity:1}}/*! a media feature in the prelude is read as a range */@media (width>=1px){.t03{color:red}}/*! a condition whose block is empty paints nothing */.t04{color:red}/*! ...but each anonymous layer is a layer of its own, so the pair stands */@layer{.t05{color:red}}@layer{.t05{color:blue}}/*! a name no table names takes no branch */@unknown-rule (color:red){.t06{color:red}}"
`;

